WEBVTT

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:09.190
The eye is just about as well constructed as the best man-made optical device.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:20.210
There's no way that we can see that the eye can have arisen by the so-called evolutionary processes that biologists have accustomed themselves to.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:28.170
That means the components for the eye, in our view, already exist and reach the Earth in that form, and that surely means there are going to be eyes elsewhere.

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:29.960
What about contacting...

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.700
other worlds, being in our other worlds.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.740
Well, in our solar system, I'm afraid there aren't any.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.160
No Martians, no little green men.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.420
But look at it this way.

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:42.290
In our galaxy, there are 100,000 million stars.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:44.790
We know 1,000 million galaxies.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:46.890
Many of these stars have planets.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.470
Therefore, they must surely be life as well

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.160
and could be contacted.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.380
The only way we can think of, by means of radio.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.740
