00:08:27.890 --> 00:08:29.910
Frank Windsor, later famous for...

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:33.540
played Fleming's treacherous colleague, Dr Bridger.

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:37.060
It really was a message, yes, from a planet, a very distant planet.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:38.520
Somewhere in Andromeda, that's right.

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:44.070
Andromeda is a constellation, and then it is the galaxy Messier 31,

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:45.950
the great Andromeda Spowl.

00:08:46.150 --> 00:08:47.750
You can just see it with the naked eye.

00:08:48.190 --> 00:08:50.330
It really is a Spowl, like a huge cat in the wheel,

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:53.960
but placed at a rather narrow angle to us, unfortunately.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:56.440
It's a galaxy bigger than our own,

00:08:56.900 --> 00:08:59.620
containing more than our quota of 100,000 million stars.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:02.560
and it's well over two million light years away.

00:09:03.220 --> 00:09:06.040
Well, that is a comfortable way away.

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:07.680
What is all this?

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:09.550
I'm coming to that.

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:14.350
I just wonder how many beings are there in the Andromeda galaxy

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:16.770
looking across at our galaxy and saying,

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:17.740
what's up there?

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:21.010
In America, you know, there was very great excitement.

00:09:21.510 --> 00:09:23.070
Everybody was very much alarmed.

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:28.020
And in Europe, in fact, everywhere in your government say,

00:09:28.590 --> 00:09:29.510
it is nothing.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.130
There is nothing we will tell you later, and people forget.

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:38.190
Basically the message that came from somewhere out of space, you know what I mean,

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:43.230
and it's on this computer, and then it's a question of where it came from and who put it there.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:44.970
What was your point, Dr Fleming?

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:49.380
That the message and all that derived from it was evil.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:50.460
Evil?

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:55.810
For us, yes. It was sent by a superior intelligence which would subjugate us.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:57.710
It would, if necessary, have destroyed us.

00:09:57.850 --> 00:09:59.950
Fleming was the assistant.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.260
to the Esmond Knight character.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:06.940
He built this computer to a certain, to a specification

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:10.980
that he'd got from these mysterious messages from outer space.

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:15.580
But Bridger was, well, he was a very unpleasant character, actually.

00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:18.770
He was not very helpful to anybody

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:24.940
because he was getting secrets out to another power.

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:26.240
Another power, yes.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:36.400
This clip from episode two was shot on the very first day of filming for the serial in June 1961.

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:42.600
Dr. Bridges' activities had aroused the suspicions of the project's PR officer,

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:47.440
actually an undercover agent of British security.

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:56.660
My character was Judy Adamson, and she seemed to me to be a rather pretty sort of person.

00:10:57.850 --> 00:10:59.980
Not really the sort of person...

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.300
I usually played at all.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:05.430
My chauffeur tells me we are being followed by a taxi.

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:07.270
Not to worry.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.580
There are always taxis in London.

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:11.300
He will see we get nowhere.

00:11:12.590 --> 00:11:14.930
What is important is that I have my call to Stuttgart.

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:16.100
Smoking?

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:17.180
No, thank you.

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:23.000
You sent us a telex message to Geneva some months ago.

00:11:23.630 --> 00:11:23.930
Yes.

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:25.850
Since when we do not hear from you?

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:27.460
Changed my mind.

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:29.960
Now perhaps the time has come to change...

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:35.250
I worked with John Hollis quite a few times, in radio as well, you know.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:36.370
Yes, he did a lot of radio.

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:38.850
Yes, I've done some radio with John as well, yeah.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.210
I think I knew him from radio when I cast him.

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:46.140
I think Andromeda was the first time I cast John in a telly.

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:47.740
How much?

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:53.260
Excuse if you want me to give you information.

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:59.950
Really, Dr. Bridger, you have no finesse.

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:11.400
Bidja was doing it because he needed to, you know, and as it happened, he got rumbled, and he came to a bit of a sticky end, I think, really.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:14.980
I don't know what happened at the bottom of the cliff, but I mean...

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:17.040
It wasn't much fun at the top.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:21.670
It was hard work getting there, actually, I remember.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:29.960
I had to climb down this cliff every morning to get to the beach, and there was no handrail or anything.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:35.140
and it was very steep, and I was terrified because I'm no good at heights.

00:12:35.540 --> 00:12:38.640
It was alright coming back in the evening because you didn't look back.

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:44.480
And the number of times that one of us, Jack May or myself, fell down

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:49.360
because it was ridden, the area was ridden with rabbit holes.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:54.460
That's right, somebody twisted their ankle, wasn't it you? Or Jack?

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:58.780
One or the other twisted an ankle, I remember that.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.140
I think it was Jack. We kept on going down.

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:05.980
Jack said, oh, God, I can't go on. Yeah, it was Jack.

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:08.410
I can't go on. He's very twisted.

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:12.330
But you couldn't, when you were running, you couldn't see the hole, you know.

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:14.470
And you put your foot in it.

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:16.070
Yeah, right.

00:13:16.530 --> 00:13:20.530
We were running down this hill, and it was getting quite late,

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:23.270
and we were all very hungry, and we thought we should stop.

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:25.850
But Michael kept making us do it again.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:29.810
And so Jack May, who was a lovely man,

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:33.510
He said to me, I'm fed up with this.

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:36.190
I'm more your drawing room sort of actor.

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:37.970
And I said, so am I.

00:13:38.370 --> 00:13:43.630
And anyway, he said, if we do it again, I'm going to pretend to fall down and hurt my leg.

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:45.380
And so we did it again.

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:51.060
And he fell down with a sort of terrible cry and then said, oh, oh, I can't get up.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:52.280
I've done my leg in.

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:54.350
And so people rushed up.

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:56.590
And then he got up and he sort of limped along.

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:59.500
And so we had to stop filming, obviously.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:02.060
and we went to a pub and had a nice dinner.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:04.580
But he still had to keep on limping, of course,

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:07.100
until the next day when it magically got better.

